Why Use Marshmallow
- Integration with Web Frameworks
Marshmallow has long been the go‑to library for Flask, Django, and SQLAlchemy projects. It integrates smoothly with ORMs, making it easy to serialize/deserialize database models.

- Schema‑based Approach
Marshmallow uses explicit schemas instead of type hints. This makes it very flexible when you want fine‑grained control over how data is represented, 
especially when working with legacy code or APIs that don’t follow strict typing.

- Serialization Focus
Marshmallow was originally built for serialization and deserialization. If your main goal is to transform Python objects into JSON (and back), 
Marshmallow is very mature and widely adopted.

- Customizability
You can easily define custom fields, pre/post processing hooks, and transformations. This makes Marshmallow powerful when dealing with complex or non‑standard data formats.
